/* PARKED 2026-08-02 -- 979/985 instructions exact, LENGTH-EXACT (99.4%).
 * Full decode; the residue is an F2 sched1 tie inside the 0x18 arm only:
 *
 *   orig  li v0,48 ; sll v1,s8,4 ; li t0,46 ; sb v0,0xA ; li v0,8 ;
 *         sb v0,0x11 ; sll v0,s8,5
 *   ours  li v0,48 ; sb v0,0xA ; li v0,8 ; sb v0,0x11 ; sll v0,s8,5 ;
 *         sll v1,s8,4 ; li t0,46
 *
 * i.e. the original front-loads the two long-lived defs (`i * 16`, feeding the
 * 0xB and 0x1C stores, and the 0x2E fx constant) ahead of the life/unk11 store
 * pair; ours defines them at their source position.  Exhausted: moving the
 * seed/fx stores earlier in the arm (the li moves with its store, 7 diffs), an
 * `i * 16` local (7 diffs -- the literal written twice is one better), a local
 * for the 0x2E constant (blows the whole function's allocation up, 969 diffs),
 * and swapping the life/z statement order (no change).  Everything else in the
 * function -- all five newly decoded arms -- is byte-identical.
 *
 * Levers that got it here:
 *  - Arms 0x46 / 0x50 must use the `int v3[3]` / `int v4[3]` STACK ARRAYS the
 *    0x47 arm uses, not scalar locals: the original reloads each component at
 *    every use (a store through `rec` invalidates the MEM), and scalar locals
 *    win hard regs instead.  v3 is shared with arms 0x47 and 0x4E; only 0x50
 *    needs a fresh array (frame 0x98 -> 0xB0 = one array + the two 8-aligned
 *    invariant spill slots).
 *  - `z = v3[2];` before the colour block in both streak arms: that is what
 *    puts the load ahead of the colours so jump.c can cross-jump the whole
 *    colour block + the b[2] tail (without it only the last three insns merge,
 *    +11 insns).
 *  - The rand-derived factor needs an explicit `(int)` cast --
 *    `func_8006272C()` is unsigned, so the >> 12 comes out `srl`.
 *  - `hi` is a NAMED local here (assigned inside the 0xC arm) so the shift is
 *    NOT hoisted; the flight overlays' copy writes it inline for the opposite
 *    reason (see func_level_11_80082F58).
 *  - 0x15 and 0x4C both want the if/else form (`x = a*2` / `x = a*2 - 0x80`),
 *    not `x = a*2; if (...) x -= 0x80;` -- the latter lets cse share the shift
 *    with the seed store two blocks later.
 *  - Store order inside 0x15 is load-bearing: r before g (g then fills the
 *    hoisted-invariant load-delay slot) and unk10 after life.
 *
 * Word-identical (bar branch displacements) to func_level_20_800861CC: landing
 * this one lands 7,880 exact bytes.  It is also the donor for the 1085-insn
 * five-overlay group (levels 1/2/4/10/28, 21,700 bytes), which needs only one
 * further arm (0x6, 100 insns) on top of these five.
 */
